{
  "$comment": [
    "Every toolchain this action can set up, keyed by the exact cl.exe build.",
    "",
    "WHY THE EXACT BUILD IS THE KEY, not the marketing version: for byte-matching",
    "work the compiler's identity IS the question. Visual C++ 2005 RTM and SP1 both",
    "stamp 50727 in the PE Rich header, so a binary cannot tell you which one built",
    "it; only the fourth component (.42 vs .762) distinguishes them, and they emit",
    "different code. Any version close to another gets its own entry here.",
    "",
    "'mirrors' is a list on purpose. These are third-party community archives and",
    "any one of them can disappear; the action tries each in order and verifies the",
    "same sha256 whichever answers. This action redistributes nothing: it points at",
    "upstream and checks what arrives.",
    "",
    "'contains' is measured, not assumed. It is there because the packs differ",
    "wildly in completeness and a missing lib/ directory is not discoverable until",
    "a build fails confusingly."
  ],
